i think we could do it easy they don't move that fast

41
00:04:13,660 --> 00:04:15,000
that's true

42
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,880
what do you think sound good

43
00:04:17,880 --> 00:04:18,840
sure

44
00:04:18,840 --> 00:04:21,360
any one of them could move

45
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:24,360
so stay alert here we go

46
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:47,820
get going

47
00:04:47,820 --> 00:04:54,820
they blocked us we can't get out of the way

48
00:04:54,820 --> 00:05:17,000
They blocked us!

49
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,720
We can't get to the other door!

50
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:20,800
What do we do now?

51
00:05:21,220 --> 00:05:23,500
There's only one thing we can do now!

52
00:05:23,500 --> 00:05:25,880
Go back the other way as fast as we can!

53
00:05:26,540 --> 00:05:27,840
Run for it!

54
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:38,960
They're unusually aggressive.

55
00:05:39,780 --> 00:05:42,060
I wonder if we did something to tick them off.

56
00:05:42,180 --> 00:05:42,820
That's silly.

57
00:05:43,620 --> 00:05:44,880
They don't have any feelings.

58
00:05:45,020 --> 00:05:46,300
They're empty suits of armor.

59
00:05:46,940 --> 00:05:50,680
The only way to stop them is to find whoever it is that's controlling them.

60
00:05:50,680 --> 00:05:54,540
If someone was controlling those things, I didn't see them.

61
00:05:55,860 --> 00:06:00,180
Usually what happens is you get too close to them and then they attack.

62
00:06:01,140 --> 00:06:04,000
But these ones, they move to block the door.

63
00:06:05,200 --> 00:06:10,060
That means there could be something on the other side of that door they have to protect.

64
00:06:10,060 --> 00:06:13,660
Like whoever or whatever is controlling them.

65
00:06:14,280 --> 00:06:15,440
That's gotta be it.

66
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:16,860
It's the only explanation.

67
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:19,740
Then you think it might be a monster?

68
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:20,840
I don't know.

69
00:06:21,140 --> 00:06:21,420
Maybe.

70
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:24,700
Normal folks wouldn't have access to magic that powerful.

71
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:26,560
What now?

72
00:06:26,740 --> 00:06:29,620
Unless we can get past them and through that door, we're stuck.

73
00:06:30,020 --> 00:06:33,500
We'll have to find the major whatever that's controlling the armor.

74
00:06:33,900 --> 00:06:36,420
Once we take them out, that should break the spell.

75
00:06:37,020 --> 00:06:37,580
Obviously.

76
00:06:37,580 --> 00:06:38,800
I got it.

77
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:44,480
If three people distract the armor, one of us can sneak right on by and get through the door.

78
00:06:47,700 --> 00:06:49,340
Good luck sneaking by.

79
00:06:50,940 --> 00:06:54,620
Actually, I thought you'd do the sneaking since that's kind of your thing.

80
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:57,100
But fighting definitely isn't my thing.

81
00:06:57,760 --> 00:07:00,520
Living armor doesn't have eyes or ears because it doesn't need them.

82
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:03,160
Stealth skills don't work on things that aren't alive.

83
00:07:03,940 --> 00:07:05,940
They don't have eyes or ears.

84
00:07:07,580 --> 00:07:12,760
Are you ready?

85
00:07:14,540 --> 00:07:15,760
Let's do this!

86
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:16,060
Yeah!

87
00:07:16,760 --> 00:07:18,500
Come on, you rusty buckets!

88
00:07:18,640 --> 00:07:19,680
I'm right here!

89
00:07:19,820 --> 00:07:20,760
Come and get me!

90
00:07:21,500 --> 00:07:21,980
Ah!

91
00:07:22,140 --> 00:07:23,080
Bad idea!

92
00:07:23,440 --> 00:07:24,480
Don't fear, missy!

93
00:07:24,480 --> 00:07:24,740
Ask them!

94
00:07:28,640 --> 00:07:29,160
Oh!

95
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:36,740
As they're mad!

96
00:07:45,740 --> 00:07:46,260
Ah!

97
00:07:46,260 --> 00:08:04,480
Oh, fantastic. There's one in here, too.

98
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:11,880
This one looks different from the armor in the other room.

99
00:08:12,620 --> 00:08:15,880
There doesn't seem to be anyone here doing the controlling.

100
00:08:16,260 --> 00:08:18,880
I get the feeling this one's the strongest.

101
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:23,580
I can't call the others for help.

102
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:28,060
I'll have to fight this thing on my own and figure out what the armors are protecting.

103
00:08:34,540 --> 00:08:38,380
I'll try chopping off an arm or a leg. Maybe that'll slow it down.

104
00:08:46,260 --> 00:08:47,400
Oh, God tiny ass.

105
00:08:47,400 --> 00:08:47,640
Oh, God.

106
00:08:48,260 --> 00:08:49,220
Oh, God!

107
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:51,640
Oh, God!

108
00:08:51,640 --> 00:08:52,960
Oh, God!

109
00:09:00,880 --> 00:09:01,640
Damn it!

110
00:09:05,780 --> 00:09:06,460
Oh...

111
00:09:06,460 --> 00:09:06,480
Oh!

112
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:13,780
It was protecting its shield.

113
00:09:14,780 --> 00:09:16,780
What the...

114
00:09:16,780 --> 00:09:20,400
What's that stuck to it?

115
00:09:21,460 --> 00:09:24,460
Wait, I've seen something like that before.

116
00:09:31,300 --> 00:09:32,520
That's right.

117
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:38,400
It's a...

118
00:09:38,400 --> 00:09:45,000
An egg case.

119
00:09:45,760 --> 00:09:47,140
That's what it was protecting.

120
00:09:48,100 --> 00:09:48,520
Eggs!

121
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:53,740
What kind of eggs are they?

122
00:09:54,200 --> 00:09:56,320
Do they belong to whatever's controlling the armor?

123
00:09:56,940 --> 00:09:59,820
Living armor doesn't have eyes or ears because it doesn't need them.

124
00:09:59,820 --> 00:10:00,940
I knew it.

125
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:02,740
There's more to these things.

126
00:10:03,460 --> 00:10:05,820
If it has no eyes or ears...

127
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:08,760
Why'd it bother picking up the helmet and straightening it?

128
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:11,520
Why'd it turn its head to track our movements?

129
00:10:13,060 --> 00:10:14,540
Why's it got eggs?

130
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:17,020
I know why.

131
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:18,680
There's a creature in it!

132
00:10:19,620 --> 00:10:22,180
There's no outside force controlling them.

133
00:10:22,700 --> 00:10:26,280
They move instinctively and deliberately to protect its eggs.

134
00:10:27,160 --> 00:10:28,220
They're alive!

135
00:10:28,220 --> 00:10:30,680
That means they can be killed.

136
00:10:31,820 --> 00:10:33,260
That means...

137
00:10:33,260 --> 00:10:35,460
We can eat them.

138
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:39,840
Take this!

139
00:10:42,640 --> 00:10:44,040
There's too many of them!

140
00:10:44,920 --> 00:10:45,800
Oh, no!

141
00:10:48,800 --> 00:10:49,740
Keep moving!

142
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:51,120
If you stop, you're dead!

143
00:10:51,220 --> 00:10:52,140
Behind you!

144
00:10:52,140 --> 00:10:53,980
Aslam!

145
00:10:55,840 --> 00:10:56,520
Wait!

146
00:10:56,800 --> 00:10:57,120
Wait!

147
00:10:57,220 --> 00:10:57,600
No!

148
00:11:00,600 --> 00:11:04,260
They can share their parts?

149
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:05,180
Not fair!

150
00:11:05,320 --> 00:11:06,340
How's that possible?

151
00:11:08,340 --> 00:11:09,860
Hurry up, Lyos!

152
00:11:09,980 --> 00:11:12,920
We're getting swarmed in here and things are moving fast!

153
00:11:12,920 --> 00:11:16,260
It doesn't stop if you chop off its head.

154
00:11:16,840 --> 00:11:19,360
But if it's a living thing, it can be killed.

155
00:11:19,980 --> 00:11:21,840
My options are slashing at its organs,

156
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:23,160
make it bleed to death,

157
00:11:23,780 --> 00:11:25,020
suffocate it, starve it.

158
00:11:25,620 --> 00:11:26,440
What am I saying?

159
00:11:26,500 --> 00:11:27,460
Those will take too long.

160
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:29,580
First things first,

161
00:11:29,660 --> 00:11:31,820
I need to find out what kind of creature's inside.

162
00:11:34,060 --> 00:11:35,220
Maybe it's a slime.

163
00:11:35,740 --> 00:11:37,020
But they don't move with precision.

164
00:11:37,220 --> 00:11:38,060
They just...

165
00:11:38,060 --> 00:11:38,440
ooze.

166
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:42,580
Maybe it's a horde of insects.

167
00:11:43,320 --> 00:11:45,880
No, I would have heard them scuttling around inside.

168
00:11:46,320 --> 00:11:48,160
Maybe there's a big spider in the helmet

169
00:11:48,160 --> 00:11:50,020
using its legs to move the armor.

170
00:11:50,880 --> 00:11:52,440
I wonder if that last one's it.

171
00:11:53,860 --> 00:11:56,000
I'm not gonna find out standing here.

172
00:11:56,900 --> 00:11:58,400
I can't overpower it,

173
00:11:58,720 --> 00:12:00,600
so I'll outsmart it.

174
00:12:01,440 --> 00:12:02,540
Yeah, this'll do.

175
00:12:03,160 --> 00:12:05,240
I'll draw its attention and get right up next to it.

176
00:12:08,440 --> 00:12:18,000
I've got it.

177
00:12:19,780 --> 00:12:20,960
Now, let's see.

178
00:12:22,420 --> 00:12:23,240
It's empty.

179
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:27,760
If there's nothing here,

180
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:30,880
why'd that other one even bother picking its helmet up?

181
00:12:32,480 --> 00:12:33,340
He's coming.

182
00:12:34,020 --> 00:12:34,400
Uh-oh.

183
00:12:34,860 --> 00:12:35,680
What do I do?

184
00:12:35,680 --> 00:12:40,100
Uh-oh.

185
00:12:41,580 --> 00:12:42,060
Wait.

186
00:12:42,480 --> 00:12:44,460
How can it not see me hiding over here?

187
00:12:45,340 --> 00:12:47,240
There's something about the helmet, then.

188
00:12:48,620 --> 00:12:49,460
What's this?

189
00:12:49,460 --> 00:13:00,960
What the heck?

190
00:13:01,300 --> 00:13:02,360
It's a mollusk.

191
00:13:02,820 --> 00:13:04,560
And right between the layers of plating.

192
00:13:05,240 --> 00:13:07,720
That's why cutting parts off the armor didn't work.

193
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:09,840
There's a colony of these in it.

194
00:13:10,660 --> 00:13:12,280
It's still looking for its head.

195
00:13:13,580 --> 00:13:14,420
All right, then.

196
00:13:15,020 --> 00:13:15,460
Here!

197
00:13:15,460 --> 00:13:15,520
Here!

198
00:13:15,520 --> 00:13:15,580
Here!

199
00:13:15,580 --> 00:13:15,600
Here!

200
00:13:19,460 --> 00:13:33,880
Now we're talking.

201
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:35,760
This must be filled with them.

202
00:13:37,580 --> 00:13:39,840
Looks like they connect to each other at the joints,

203
00:13:40,060 --> 00:13:42,580
then expand and contract like muscles to move around.

204
00:13:43,300 --> 00:13:44,880
But which one laid the eggs?

205
00:13:45,340 --> 00:13:46,760
Guess if they're hermaphrodites,

206
00:13:46,760 --> 00:13:47,780
guess they all could have laid them.

207
00:13:49,520 --> 00:13:51,340
Now's not the time to think about that.

208
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:53,480
Gimme!

209
00:13:54,540 --> 00:13:56,660
Let go already!

210
00:13:57,440 --> 00:13:58,220
Hey, guys!

211
00:13:58,380 --> 00:13:59,320
Get over here!

212
00:13:59,560 --> 00:14:00,960
Do we look like we can?

213
00:14:06,100 --> 00:14:06,620
Huh?

214
00:14:06,620 --> 00:14:12,900
What was that?

215
00:14:12,900 --> 00:14:14,440
And why did they go chasing it?

216
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:15,920
Whoa!

217
00:14:16,520 --> 00:14:18,800
So, it was a mage after all.

218
00:14:18,960 --> 00:14:20,380
Nope, there was no mage.

219
00:14:20,940 --> 00:14:23,620
This so-called living armor isn't controlled by magic,

220
00:14:23,980 --> 00:14:25,440
but by the creatures inside.

221
00:14:26,020 --> 00:14:26,520
Huh?

222
00:14:26,900 --> 00:14:27,920
Check this out.

223
00:14:28,340 --> 00:14:29,660
The armor has two layers,

224
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:31,320
and look what's sandwiched between them.

225
00:14:33,180 --> 00:14:34,900
That makes the armor move.

226
00:14:34,900 --> 00:14:38,900
In the armor,

227
00:14:39,140 --> 00:14:40,280
these things link together.

228
00:14:40,740 --> 00:14:43,420
They form groups that act just like the muscles do in our bodies.

229
00:14:45,280 --> 00:14:46,780
On their own, they're weak.

230
00:14:47,060 --> 00:14:49,160
But together, they use the armor like a structure,

231
00:14:49,340 --> 00:14:49,800
and that

232
00:14:49,800 --> 00:14:52,060
is how they can move like us.

233
00:14:53,520 --> 00:14:54,900
They were aggressive with us

234
00:14:54,900 --> 00:14:57,260
because we happened to show up after they laid their eggs.

235
00:14:58,080 --> 00:14:58,520
Seriously?

236
00:14:59,020 --> 00:15:00,980
Those icky things hatch from eggs?

237
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:03,260
Born from eggs!

238
00:15:03,260 --> 00:15:04,100
Isn't that amazing?

239
00:15:04,540 --> 00:15:06,580
And I'm the one who found out about their secrets?

240
00:15:06,880 --> 00:15:07,400
Until now,

241
00:15:07,500 --> 00:15:09,640
everyone thought living armor was controlled by magic.

242
00:15:09,920 --> 00:15:11,520
Wait till we tell the world about them.

243
00:15:11,680 --> 00:15:12,820
We're gonna blow some mines!

244
00:15:13,880 --> 00:15:14,900
You see that?

245
00:15:15,260 --> 00:15:16,760
How when he talks about monsters,

246
00:15:16,880 --> 00:15:18,040
he gets crazy eyes?

247
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:19,380
Creeps me out.

248
00:15:19,560 --> 00:15:21,300
Hey, don't be rude.

249
00:15:22,100 --> 00:15:22,580
Senshi,

250
00:15:22,820 --> 00:15:24,040
we can't eat the armor,

251
00:15:24,220 --> 00:15:25,660
but I bet we can eat these guys.

252
00:15:25,660 --> 00:15:28,100
They look pretty dang nutritious, don't they?

253
00:15:28,280 --> 00:15:28,700
Huh?

254
00:15:31,580 --> 00:15:34,940
There's no way anyone's eating that mysterious gooey gunk!

255
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:36,220
Oh, Marcel.

256
00:15:36,680 --> 00:15:39,240
The first bite of a new food is always mysterious.

257
00:15:39,580 --> 00:15:40,600
Where's your sense of adventure?

258
00:15:42,780 --> 00:15:44,500
That's a stupid adventure!

259
00:15:44,920 --> 00:15:45,820
I'll fix him up.

260
00:15:47,160 --> 00:15:48,520
Never cooked him before,

261
00:15:48,680 --> 00:15:50,400
so can't promise it'll be any good.

262
00:15:50,800 --> 00:15:52,120
Aw, thank you, Senshi.

263
00:15:52,780 --> 00:15:53,900
Hell no!

264
00:15:54,420 --> 00:15:56,480
What if those things are loaded with poison?

265
00:15:57,120 --> 00:15:59,540
I'm pretty sure any creature that poisonous

266
00:15:59,540 --> 00:16:01,720
wouldn't bother with hiding in a suit of armor.

267
00:16:02,680 --> 00:16:05,100
What the heck kind of meal do I make out of him?

268
00:16:06,020 --> 00:16:06,960
See that part?

269
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:09,060
When I tried to pry it open with my hand,

270
00:16:09,140 --> 00:16:09,780
it wouldn't open.

271
00:16:10,440 --> 00:16:12,660
I ended up making a cut right along there.

272
00:16:12,900 --> 00:16:14,100
It couldn't close after that.

273
00:16:14,760 --> 00:16:17,220
You know how a mollusk has that adductor muscle thing

274
00:16:17,220 --> 00:16:18,040
to close their shells?

275
00:16:18,360 --> 00:16:19,240
That's what that is.

276
00:16:19,640 --> 00:16:21,340
So these are like shellfish.

277
00:16:22,120 --> 00:16:23,760
I got an idea.

278
00:16:24,180 --> 00:16:26,280
We'll need to pry him out of the armor first.

279
00:16:33,920 --> 00:16:34,720
Oh, no.

280
00:16:35,400 --> 00:16:35,960
They drowned.

281
00:16:36,580 --> 00:16:38,800
Guess we can't clean off the sand that way.

282
00:16:39,620 --> 00:16:41,080
And they didn't come from the sea,

283
00:16:41,280 --> 00:16:42,580
so maybe we don't need to.

284
00:16:43,560 --> 00:16:45,620
Not sure if its organs are safe to eat,

285
00:16:45,720 --> 00:16:47,020
so they're going in the trash.

286
00:16:47,020 --> 00:16:50,740
I'll slice these ones up and make soup.

287
00:16:51,160 --> 00:16:52,360
Then heat some oil,

288
00:16:53,100 --> 00:16:56,280
add critter, season in the medicinal herbs for a stir-fry.

289
00:16:56,280 --> 00:17:04,080
The helmet critter is steamed.

290
00:17:04,080 --> 00:17:08,120
And these, classic style all the way.

291
00:17:15,340 --> 00:17:16,140
It's ready!

292
00:17:16,140 --> 00:17:26,400
What are you going to try first?

293
00:17:26,740 --> 00:17:29,960
Uh, uh, soup, I guess.

294
00:17:30,360 --> 00:17:32,860
Wait, does anyone have an antidote for food poisoning?

295
00:17:33,520 --> 00:17:35,200
Well, it doesn't smell bad.

296
00:17:35,940 --> 00:17:38,100
Pretty sure what I'm smelling is iron.

297
00:17:38,980 --> 00:17:39,480
Lyos.

298
00:17:39,480 --> 00:17:49,320
Why is everyone looking at me like that?

299
00:17:49,840 --> 00:17:51,580
You wanted to eat living armor,

300
00:17:51,780 --> 00:17:52,680
so there it is.

301
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:53,160
Eat up.

302
00:17:53,300 --> 00:17:54,320
You discovered him.

303
00:17:54,460 --> 00:17:55,700
You get the first bite.

304
00:17:56,120 --> 00:17:56,920
Such an honor.

305
00:17:57,720 --> 00:17:59,420
You leave his corpse if he dies, okay?

306
00:17:59,800 --> 00:18:00,100
Okay.

307
00:18:00,100 --> 00:18:07,040
Did he die?

308
00:18:07,540 --> 00:18:08,420
It's delicious!

309
00:18:09,500 --> 00:18:10,940
Oh, my God, the flavor!

310
00:18:11,220 --> 00:18:12,300
It's so good!

311
00:18:12,560 --> 00:18:14,600
It didn't taste like anything at first but then!

312
00:18:14,740 --> 00:18:15,620
Oh, man!

313
00:18:16,280 --> 00:18:19,040
How long does food poisoning take to make you sick?

314
00:18:19,500 --> 00:18:20,560
Depends on the food.

315
00:18:20,560 --> 00:18:20,960
Ah!

316
00:18:25,600 --> 00:18:26,660
Not bad.

317
00:18:27,320 --> 00:18:29,300
Could use a condiment or three, maybe.

318
00:18:29,300 --> 00:18:30,940
How'd those come out?

319
00:18:31,540 --> 00:18:31,700
Huh?

320
00:18:32,300 --> 00:18:33,540
Uh...

321
00:18:33,540 --> 00:18:37,380
Well, at least these were stir-fried with medicinal herbs.

322
00:18:38,640 --> 00:18:38,780
Oh!

323
00:18:39,540 --> 00:18:39,720
Mm.

324
00:18:40,560 --> 00:18:41,160
Mm-hmm.

325
00:18:42,080 --> 00:18:43,020
Uh, and?

326
00:18:43,780 --> 00:18:45,380
It doesn't taste bad.

327
00:18:46,260 --> 00:18:47,420
Uh...

328
00:18:47,420 --> 00:18:48,300
Oh...

329
00:18:50,300 --> 00:18:52,300
Uh...

330
00:18:52,300 --> 00:18:53,300
Uh...

331
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:57,300
Oh...

332
00:18:57,300 --> 00:18:59,580
How is it, Marsil?

333
00:18:59,980 --> 00:19:00,540
They...

334
00:19:00,540 --> 00:19:02,960
kind of taste like mushrooms.

335
00:19:03,340 --> 00:19:04,060
I know, right?

336
00:19:05,400 --> 00:19:07,400
I'm trying the steamed ones next.

337
00:19:07,880 --> 00:19:10,480
I bet these'll taste better than the grilled ones.

338
00:19:10,540 --> 00:19:11,220
Wow.

339
00:19:13,420 --> 00:19:14,580
Tastes like mold.

340
00:19:15,220 --> 00:19:17,540
Guess the helmet stink got cooked into them.

341
00:19:17,540 --> 00:19:17,980
What?

342
00:19:20,980 --> 00:19:21,420
Here.

343
00:19:21,920 --> 00:19:22,180
Hmm.

344
00:19:23,280 --> 00:19:26,080
In all my years of eating monster in this here dungeon,

345
00:19:26,420 --> 00:19:29,160
I never would have dreamed I'd eat critters like those.

346
00:19:29,580 --> 00:19:32,940
I doubt anyone dreamed living armor was really a type of shellfish.

347
00:19:33,380 --> 00:19:35,280
A weird type born from an egg case.

348
00:19:35,960 --> 00:19:38,580
Wouldn't it be neat to see what they're like right when they hatch?

349
00:19:39,240 --> 00:19:41,440
I bet they're so small you can barely see them.

350
00:19:41,440 --> 00:19:45,600
As they mature, they form their outer shells and find others like them.

351
00:19:45,960 --> 00:19:49,340
They figure out how to move, start exploring, make colonies.

352
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:53,580
Maybe they line up like we saw them right before they mate.

353
00:19:54,320 --> 00:19:56,220
Something tells me they're hermaphrodites,

354
00:19:56,300 --> 00:19:58,940
and the biggest, healthiest colony lays all the eggs.

355
00:19:59,800 --> 00:20:01,460
Wait, I just thought of something.

356
00:20:02,120 --> 00:20:04,000
Whenever I saw suits of armor holding hands,

357
00:20:04,180 --> 00:20:05,500
I thought it was a dungeon prank,

358
00:20:05,580 --> 00:20:06,980
but maybe that was a mating ritual.

359
00:20:07,620 --> 00:20:08,660
Someone needs a nap.

360
00:20:08,660 --> 00:20:12,660
I was scared of living armor for so long.

361
00:20:13,140 --> 00:20:16,440
Turns out, it was just a fragile, delicious monster.

362
00:20:17,400 --> 00:20:19,720
Hey, I'm sorry your old sword got broken.

363
00:20:20,300 --> 00:20:21,660
That one's pretty neat, though.

364
00:20:21,940 --> 00:20:22,300
Hmm.

365
00:20:25,900 --> 00:20:26,900
Hey, Lyos.

366
00:20:27,620 --> 00:20:28,920
If you're taking that,

367
00:20:29,020 --> 00:20:30,860
want me to check it to make sure it's not cursed?

368
00:20:31,320 --> 00:20:32,600
No! Don't trouble yourself!

369
00:20:32,940 --> 00:20:34,400
It's not cursed at all, really!

370
00:20:34,660 --> 00:20:35,620
Totally not cursed!

371
00:20:35,840 --> 00:20:36,980
Like you can tell.

372
00:20:36,980 --> 00:20:40,280
Don't blame me if it turns out you get cursed.

373
00:20:43,380 --> 00:20:44,640
Wait up! I'm coming!

374
00:20:46,140 --> 00:20:48,280
So, with a new sword in hand,

375
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:49,880
the journey continues.

376
00:20:51,840 --> 00:20:53,800
And as they descend into the dungeon,

377
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:55,960
the other three have no idea

378
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:58,400
their party has gained a new member.

379
00:20:58,400 --> 00:21:01,060
It's arock of death.

380
00:21:09,800 --> 00:21:11,400
And is that a new demon?

381
00:21:13,420 --> 00:21:15,620
Oh, H information.

382
00:21:15,700 --> 00:21:17,700
This is a new demon quiER pharmacy.

383
00:21:17,880 --> 00:21:19,540
What are you kidding me?

